---
/**
 * /careers/ — hiring page. Content verbatim from the live page.
 *
 * Section band archetype: hero → Why Join (2-col: heading+diamond | 4 items) →
 * Our Values (intro + 7-item 2-col grid) → Open Positions (dim band, dynamic
 * Workable listing via @elements/JobBoard) → "Get notified" form CTA → dark
 * "More ways to get involved" band → footer.
 *
 * Measure ladder (live): hero centered col-8; Why Join + Our Values are a
 * centered col-8 block, left-aligned internally; both value/why grids are 2-up.
 */
import Page from '@layouts/Page.astro';
import SimpleHero from '@components/sections/hero/SimpleHero.astro';
import ContentSection from '@components/sections/ContentSection.astro';
import CtaSection from '@components/sections/cta/CtaSection.astro';
import ButtonCta from '@components/sections/cta/ButtonCta.astro';
import JobBoard from '@elements/JobBoard.astro';
import FormEmbed from '@elements/FormEmbed.astro';
import Button from '@ui/Button.astro';

const whyJoin = [
  { title: 'Make a real-world impact', body: 'Contribute to cutting-edge technology that addresses one of the biggest challenges in AI – accessing data responsibly.' },
  { title: 'Be part of a passionate community', body: 'Collaborate with talented engineers, researchers, and advocates from around the world who are shaping the future of privacy-preserving AI.' },
  { title: 'Grow and learn', body: 'Engage in challenging projects, learn from experienced mentors, and contribute to open-source software used by leading organizations worldwide.' },
  { title: 'Thrive in a supportive environment', body: 'We offer a flexible and collaborative work environment that values continuous learning and personal growth' },
];

const values = [
  { title: 'Mission-Driven', body: 'The mission comes first. Whoever builds the infrastructure for non-public information will shape how power over AI is distributed for decades. We exist to make sure that infrastructure is open, auditable, and publicly governed. That responsibility informs every decision we make, undistracted by other popular priorities (revenue, social credit, influence, etc.). When something doesn’t serve the mission, we let it go.' },
  { title: 'Never Give Up', body: 'We chose one of the hardest problems in technology. Progress is not linear, funding is not guaranteed, and the easy path is almost never the right one. We stay in the fight. When a technical approach fails 999 times, we build the 1000th. When a door closes, we find a window. Persistence here is not stubbornness. It’s the understanding that the problems worth solving don’t yield to half-hearted effort.' },
  { title: 'Elite Collaboration', body: 'We are an elite team focused on collaborative performance. Great remote collaboration requires communicating exactly the right amount using the right tool or venue, especially the discipline to write things down. We build trust through reliability rather than proximity. We default to public channels over private threads, and documentation over tribal knowledge.' },
  { title: 'Pragmatic Ingenuity', body: 'We invent, and then we ship. Our mission demands genuine creativity: new technical approaches, novel system architectures, and unconventional partnerships. But creativity without follow-through is just ideas. We pressure-test our innovations against real constraints (compute budgets, user needs, deployment timelines, etc.). We do the unglamorous work to get there, and choose the solution that works over the solution that merely sounds smart. The best idea is the one that actually gets used.' },
  { title: 'Candor', body: 'We say the thing. If a project is off track, we name it. If we disagree, we speak up directly, respectfully, and in the moment. We value truth over comfort and feedback over silence. In a remote organization, where you can’t read body language across a table, honest communication is how we stay aligned. It’s how we earn trust, and how we keep it.' },
  { title: 'Bias to Action', body: 'Uncertainty is our default operating environment. The playbook for building a public network for non-public information doesn’t exist yet; we’re writing it. In that context, waiting for certainty is the riskiest choice. We make the best decision we can with the information we have, move, and learn. We trust each other to act without asking permission for every step. Speed with course-correction beats precision with paralysis.' },
  { title: 'Humility', body: 'Each person walks in the authority given to them by their role in the team. This is not a false humility wherein a person pretends to lack capability, nor is it a haughtiness driven by the need to be seen or praised by others (although that praise might come). No, each person receives the authority of their role during the time they hold it, and they execute that role without hesitation.' },
];
---

<Page
  title="Careers at OpenMined"
  description="Do you dream of a future where AI benefits humanity while respecting individual privacy? Join OpenMined — a non-profit building the public network for non-public information."
>
  <SimpleHero heading="Careers at OpenMined">
    <p>Do you dream of a future where artificial intelligence benefits humanity while respecting individual privacy? At OpenMined, we’re building the tools to make that dream a reality.</p>
    <p>As a non-profit foundation, we’re dedicated to building the public network for non-public information, by creating and evangelizing open-source technology that empowers data owners to share their data without compromising privacy, security, or intellectual property.</p>
    <Button href="#open-positions" slot="actions">View open positions</Button>
  </SimpleHero>

  <!-- Why Join? — heading + diamond in the left column, 4 items on the right -->
  <section class="why">
    <div class="container why__container">
      <div class="why__grid">
        <div class="why__aside">
          <h3>Why Join?</h3>
          <img class="why__mark" src="/logos/OpenMined-Icon.svg" alt="" width="280" height="280" data-fade />
        </div>
        <div class="why__items">
          {whyJoin.map((i) => (
            <div class="why__item">
              <h5>{i.title}</h5>
              <p>{i.body}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Our Values -->
  <ContentSection
    heading="Our Values"
    as="h3"
    align="left"
    width="col-8"
    headGap="tight"
    intro="Our organization operates with a set of core values that define our identity and guide our conduct. These values are central to how we interact with each other, our partners, and our broader community."
  >
    <div class="values">
      {values.map((v) => (
        <div class="values__item">
          <h5>{v.title}</h5>
          <p>{v.body}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </ContentSection>

  <!-- Open Positions — dynamic Workable listing on a dim band -->
  <ContentSection surface="dim" heading="Open Positions" as="h3" align="left" width="col-8">
    <JobBoard />
  </ContentSection>

  <!-- Get notified when there's a new position -->
  <CtaSection
    variant="gradient"
    heading="Get notified when there's a new position"
    body="Subscribe to get the latest on fellowships, internships, contributor roles, and full-time positions at OpenMined."
  >
    <FormEmbed slot="form" formId="7d2f1f37-20b1-4ead-9996-f1e6b401b533" />
    <Fragment slot="fineprint">
      <p>Subscribing will opt you in to Hiring &amp; Recruitment Emails. Want to change that later? Just use the link at the bottom of any email.</p>
      <p>Subscribing also confirms you agree with our <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>
    </Fragment>
  </CtaSection>

  <!-- More ways to get involved -->
  <ButtonCta surface="dark" heading="More ways to get involved">
    <Button href="/get-involved/">Learn more</Button>
  </ButtonCta>
</Page>

<style>
  /* ── Why Join? ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .why { margin-block: var(--spacing-full); }
  .why__container { max-width: var(--col-8); }
  .why__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--spacing-4XL);
    align-items: center;
  }
  .why__mark {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 280px;
    height: auto;
    margin-top: var(--spacing-2XL);
  }
  .why__items {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-3XL);
  }
  .why__item h5 { margin-bottom: var(--spacing-S); }
  .why__item p { margin: 0; }

  /* ── Our Values grid ───────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .values {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--spacing-4XL) var(--spacing-3XL);
  }
  .values__item h5 { margin-bottom: var(--spacing-S); }
  .values__item p { margin: 0; }

  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .why__grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--spacing-3XL); }
    .why__mark { max-width: 200px; margin-inline: auto; }
    .values { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--spacing-3XL); }
  }
</style>
